## The chart table

::bg{location="radio_room" time="afternoon"}
::use{component="enter" who="ines" side="left" instance="use-001"}
@ines{code="0010" emotion="neutral"}: Sit. Your mornings, my charts. A ridge of high pressure coming in off the Atlantic — see how the isobars open out?
@ines{code="0020"}: The question is whether it holds until Sunday night, or breaks on Saturday like it did in '94.

<branch id="call" prompt="She slides the pen over to you.">
  <choice id="clear" text="Forecast clear skies for Sunday night">
    @ines{code="0030" emotion="fond"}: Brave. Your numbers back you. Sign it.
  </choice>
  <choice id="cautious" text="Forecast clear, with a chance of wind after midnight">
    @ines{code="0040" emotion="happy"}: That's a forecaster's answer. Honest and a little cowardly. Sign it.
  </choice>
</branch>

::set{run.forecastWritten = true}
@ines{code="0050"}: Now it has to get down the mountain before Friday is over. The radio doesn't count; Maren wants paper.
